\ ***************************************************************************
\ STARGLIDER for the BBC Master - the frame (decision 14, docs/plan.md
\ section 4)
\
\ The game owns the machine: its interrupt handler counts the fields and
\ shows each frame from the field after it's drawn. The game steps on the
\ field count, one step every STEP_FIELDS fields (decision 4), and draws a
\ frame of the latest state between steps, into the screen not shown. A
\ step is the list phase then the game's logic, as an ST frame is without
\ its drawing, since the logic reads the lists; the last step before a
\ frame draws it between the two, which is the ST's own order (its
\ world_render, then the logic), so a frame shows what the ST drew at that
\ step. What the ST's logic draws into that frame as it runs (the enemies'
\ lasers, the mines' messages, the player's bolt) goes on after the
\ step's logic (call 2, option B: in force until Matt says otherwise), so
\ the frame is shown only then (frame_show).
\
\ The game supplies step_lists and step_logic, which calls frame_show once
\ its frame's logic is done, and view_under: the draw phase's drawing
\ besides the objects (the gunsight, the ground dots).
\ ***************************************************************************

STEP_FIELDS = 4                     ; decision 4: 12.5 steps a second
MAX_STEPS   = 4                     ; a frame's most: more, and the game slows
ASSERT SHOTS >= 4 * MAX_STEPS           ; every shot a frame's steps fire kept for it (vars.6502)

\ The palette split at the view's bottom edge (decision 3): only logical
\ colour 3 changes, the view's (VIEW_COLOUR_3) to the panel's
\ (PANEL_COLOUR_3), so its four ULA entries (10, 11, 14 and 15: MODE 1
\ picks among a logical colour's four by the pixels beside it) are
\ written in the horizontal blank before the panel's first scan line.
\ User VIA T1 times it, running free at the field's period from a start in
\ step with the vertical sync (start.6502's install_irq), so that it comes
\ at the same place on the raster every field, however long anything
\ holds off the sync's interrupt. The entries' bytes for each side are in
\ c3_ula (c3_set's), which the front end, whose screens have no split,
\ makes the same (front_main.6502's palette_set): the split goes on
\ beneath it, as sound_tick and the speech's tick time themselves by it.
VIEW_COLOUR_3  = 7                  ; white
PANEL_COLOUR_3 = 4                  ; blue
PANEL_LINE     = VIEW_YMAX + 1
\ The raster: the vertical sync begins SYNC_TO_TOP scan lines before the
\ screen's first (screen_mode's R7), and the System VIA flags it at its
\ end, VSYNC_LINES on (the MOS's sync width, R3, and CA1's falling edge,
\ its PCR); a field is MODE 1's 39 character rows of 8 lines (the MOS's R4
\ and R9) with no adjust (R5), and no half line, as screen_mode turns
\ interlace off. (tools/fieldcheck.mjs measures them on jsbeeb's CRTC.)
SYNC_TO_TOP    = (39 - (34 - (32 - SCREEN_ROWS) DIV 2)) * 8
VSYNC_LINES    = 2
SCAN_US        = 64
FIELD_US       = 39 * 8 * SCAN_US
\ SPLIT_LEAD: T1 reaches 0 that many microseconds before the panel's first
\ line, the time the split's interrupt takes to its writes, set so that
\ they land in the middle of the blank. SPLIT_HOLD: the writes wait until
\ that long after T1's 0, the interrupt's quickest way to them, as a tick
\ that waited for the split and hands it on (sound.6502, speech_tick.6502)
\ comes sooner. Both measured on jsbeeb's full video (docs/journal.md, "The
\ split in step with the raster", 2026-10-19), and tools/fieldcheck.mjs
\ checks where the writes land: -D SPLIT_SWEEP=n builds with n for
\ SPLIT_LEAD, and main.6502's split_test.
IF DEFINED(SPLIT_SWEEP)
    SPLIT_LEAD = SPLIT_SWEEP
ELSE
    SPLIT_LEAD = 49
ENDIF
SPLIT_HOLD = 22
\ T1's count from the sync's flag to the split's moment, and its latch, a
\ field's (a count of n times out n + 2 microseconds on, the VIA's
\ free-running period)
SPLIT_SYNC  = (SYNC_TO_TOP - VSYNC_LINES + PANEL_LINE) * SCAN_US - SPLIT_LEAD - 2
SPLIT_LATCH = FIELD_US - 2
\ (the hold reads the count's low byte alone, which turns over
\ LO(SPLIT_LATCH) microseconds after T1's 0: a split held off longer would
\ wait a turn more, which the soak would find, but nothing holds it off
\ half so long)
ASSERT LO(SPLIT_LATCH) >= SPLIT_HOLD + 128

\ (start.6502's install_irq puts irq_handler on IRQ1V, once.)

\ irq_handler: the split, when T1 comes; at each vertical sync the view's
\ colours back, the field counted, a frame drawn shown from it, by
\ ACCCON's D (TSB and TRB, which the line drawer's X changes can't
\ split), with its colour 0 (decision 24: the ST writes its flash as its
\ frame is shown), the controls read (input.6502) and the sound's field
\ (sound.6502); between, the title song's bass and tick while it plays
\ (song_irq.6502), and the sound effect's ticks, on System VIA T1 while
\ one plays. While a clip of speech plays, the speech's interrupt comes
\ first and passes the rest on here (speech.6502). It must lie below
\ &3000, which X moves to shadow RAM.
.irq_handler
{
    ZA_INTERRUPT
    TXA : PHA
.dispatch
    BIT usrvia_ifr : BVC not_split              ; (T1 is bit 6)
.hold
    LDA usrvia_t1cl                             ; acknowledged
    CMP #LO(SPLIT_LATCH - SPLIT_HOLD) + 1 : BCS hold
    FOR i = 0..3
        LDA c3_ula + C3_PANEL + i : STA ula_pal
    NEXT
    JMP done
.not_split
    LDA song_on : BEQ not_song                  ; the title song's, out of play (song_irq.6502)
    JSR song_irq : BCS done                     ; (another waiting comes in again by IRQ1V:
.not_song                                       ; the end screen's band_irq takes the sync)
    LDA ta_kind : BEQ not_sound                 ; (the OS left T1 running)
    BIT sysvia_ifr : BVC not_sound
    JSR sound_tick
    BIT usrvia_ifr : BVS dispatch               ; a split come meanwhile at once
    BRA done
.not_sound
    LDA sysvia_ifr : AND #2 : BEQ done
    STA sysvia_ifr                              ; acknowledged
    FOR i = 0..3
        LDA c3_ula + C3_VIEW + i : STA ula_pal
    NEXT
    INC fields
    LDA frame_ready : BEQ shown
    STZ frame_ready
    LDA flash_pending : EOR #7                  ; the ULA takes the colour EORed with 7
    FOR e = {0, 1, 4, 5}                        ; logical 0's entries
        ORA #e * 16 : STA ula_pal : AND #7
    NEXT
    STZ flash_pending
    LDA #ACCCON_D
    LDX draw_buffer : BEQ show_main
    TSB acccon
    BRA shown
.show_main
    TRB acccon
.shown
    JSR input_irq
    JSR sound_vsync
.done
    PLA : TAX
    LDA &FC                                     ; the interrupted A, which the OS kept
    RTI
}
ASSERT irq_handler < &3000

\ c3_set: logical colour 3 physical colour A on the split's side X
\ (C3_VIEW above it, C3_PANEL below), as its four entries' bytes for the
\ ULA (c3_ula), which the interrupt writes as they are.
C3_VIEW  = 0
C3_PANEL = 4
.c3_set
{
    ZA_AUTO1 c
    EOR #7 : STA c                              ; (the ULA takes it EORed with 7)
    LDY #3
.entry
    LDA c3_entries,Y : ORA c : STA c3_ula,X
    INX : DEY : BPL entry
    RTS
.c3_entries
    EQUB 15 * 16, 14 * 16, 11 * 16, 10 * 16
}

\ engine_run: the game, for ever: every step that's due, and between them
\ a frame. The fields counter wraps; a frame is far shorter than 256 fields.
.engine_run
{
.wait
    JSR disc_step                               ; a read goes on while it waits
    LDA fields : SEC : SBC stepped
    CMP #STEP_FIELDS : BCC wait
    \ the steps due, no more than MAX_STEPS: past that, the game slows
    LSR A : LSR A
    ASSERT STEP_FIELDS = 4
    CMP #MAX_STEPS + 1 : BCC counted
    LDA fields : SEC : SBC #MAX_STEPS * STEP_FIELDS : STA stepped
    LDA #MAX_STEPS
.counted
    STA steps_due
.step
    LDA stepped : CLC : ADC #STEP_FIELDS : STA stepped
    JSR step_lists
    DEC steps_due : BNE logic
    JSR frame                                   ; the last step's frame
.logic
    JSR step_logic
    JSR docked_step                             ; (docked.6502)
    INC steps : BNE counted_step
    INC steps+1
.counted_step
    LDA steps_due : BNE step
    BRA wait
}

\ frame: the lists' objects drawn into the screen not shown, and the panel
\ as the ST's world_render draws it from them, for frame_show to show.
.frame
{
.shown
    JSR disc_step
    LDA frame_ready : BNE shown                 ; the last frame not yet up
    LDA draw_buffer : EOR #1 : STA draw_buffer
    TAX : LDA buffer_bank,X : STA draw_bank
    JSR screen_erase                            ; (code.6502)
.erased
    JSR draw_begin
    JSR view_under
    JSR view_objects
    JSR draw_end
    JSR panel_draw                              ; (cockpit.6502)
    LDA #&FF : STA frame_drawn
    RTS
.buffer_bank
    EQUB 0, ACCCON_X                            ; main RAM's screen, shadow's
}

\ frame_show: the frame this step drew, if it drew one, with what the
\ step's logic draws on it (view_overlays) and the texts the ST prints on
\ it (panel_texts: draw_buffer and draw_bank name its screen), shown from
\ the next vertical sync.
.frame_show
{
    LDA frame_drawn : BEQ done
    STZ frame_drawn
    JSR view_overlays
    JSR panel_texts                             ; (cockpit.6502)
    LDA #1 : STA frame_ready
    INC frames : BNE done
    INC frames+1
.done
    RTS
}

\ pause_begin, pause_end: round what runs fields of its own inside a step
\ (decision 17: the cheat prompt's waits, Interrogate's frames), so that
\ the engine discards the fields it took, as if none had passed: no steps
\ follow to catch up. (The count wraps as the fields counter does.)
.pause_begin
    LDA fields : STA paused_at
    RTS
.pause_end
    LDA fields : SEC : SBC paused_at
    CLC : ADC stepped : STA stepped
    RTS

\ wait_key (the ST's &00C0C): the next key made, as get_key has it, with
\ no end to the wait: the cheat prompt's first, in effect a pause; and
\ wait_key_timeout (&00BCA): the same, or &0D, the latch cleared, once
\ KEY_WAIT fields have passed (counted in 16 bits). Each from the logic's
\ bank, which get_key needs; the disc's read moves on meanwhile.
KEY_WAIT = &5DC + 1                             ; (the ST's waits end at the first VBL past their count)
.wait_key
{
    JSR pause_begin
.wait
    JSR disc_step
    LDA key_latch : BEQ wait
    JSR pause_end
    JMP get_key
}
.wait_key_timeout
{
    LDA #LO(KEY_WAIT) : STA key_wait_left
    LDA #HI(KEY_WAIT) : STA key_wait_left+1
    JSR pause_begin
    LDA fields : STA key_wait_at
.wait
    JSR disc_step
    LDA fields : CMP key_wait_at : BEQ polled
    STA key_wait_at
    LDA key_wait_left : BNE count
    DEC key_wait_left+1
.count
    DEC key_wait_left
    LDA key_wait_left : ORA key_wait_left+1 : BEQ out
.polled
    LDA key_latch : BEQ wait
    JSR pause_end
    JMP get_key
.out
    STZ key_latch
    JSR pause_end
    LDA #&0D
    RTS
}
